      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 1349560413}
    - target: {fileID: 4280900825574770516, guid: 5d1623387756b224fa0dcb0162e8a627, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Virus.pictureObj
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 1983196955}
    - target: {fileID: 4280900825574770516, guid: 5d1623387756b224fa0dcb0162e8a627, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Fungi.description
      value: Fungi were once silent scavengers that thrived on decay, breaking down
        what was already dead and returning it to the ground. When imbalance spread
        across the land, they evolved into something more dangerous feeding not only
        on rot, but on weakness itself. Wherever battles leave scars, Fungi grow
        rapidly, releasing invisible spores that drain strength and slow resistance
        from anything nearby. They do not attack with force, but with persistence,
        spreading quietly, overwhelming defenses over time, and turning neglect into
        collapse. In this world, Fungi are a reminder that what is ignored for too
        long can become the hardest threat to remove.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4280900825574770516, guid: 5d1623387756b224fa0dcb0162e8a627, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Virus.description
      value: Virus are the smallest enemies on the battlefield, yet the most deceptive.
        Invisible to the naked eye, they slip through defenses with ease, hijacking
        what they touch and forcing it to serve their own replication. Unlike other
        threats, Virus do not rely on strength or numbers alone they rely on speed,
        mutation, and surprise. Once they breach a line, they adapt rapidly, becoming
        harder to contain with every moment they survive. In this world, Virus embody
        the danger of unseen threats, proving that even the smallest enemy can cause
        the greatest collapse if left unchecked.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4280900825574770516, guid: 5d1623387756b224fa0dcb0162e8a627, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Helminth.pictureObj
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 443943742}
    - target: {fileID: 4280900825574770516, guid: 5d1623387756b224fa0dcb0162e8a627, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Protozoa.pictureObj
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 1673198972}
    - target: {fileID: 4280900825574770516, guid: 5d1623387756b224fa0dcb0162e8a627, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Helminth.description
      value: Helminth are massive parasitic creatures that advance slowly but relentlessly,
        burrowing through the battlefield with unwavering persistence. They do not
        rush their prey instead, they drain resources and stability over time, weakening
        defenses from within. Protected by thick layers and sheer endurance, Helminth
        are difficult to eliminate once they take hold. Their presence turns long
        battles into wars of attrition, where patience favors the enemy. In this
        world, Helminth symbolize the danger of prolonged neglect, showing that threats
        allowed to grow quietly can become nearly impossible to remove.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4280900825574770516, guid: 5d1623387756b224fa0dcb0162e8a627, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Protozoa.description
      value: "Protozoa are ancient lifeforms that existed long before the battlefield
        was ever formed, surviving through constant adaptation and cunning. Unlike
        mindless threats, they move with intention, sensing openings and exploiting
        weak points in defenses. Protozoa thrive in unstable environments, shifting
        their behavior when threatened and retreating only to strike again from a
        safer angle. Their strength lies not in raw power, but in intelligence and
        survival instinct, making them unpredictable opponents. In this world, Protozoa
        represent resilience through adaptation\u2014enemies that endure by learning
        how to survive every encounter."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
